3. Pages regex matched `id="page-title"` and `id="page-sub"` too — false positives ("title","sub"). Real pages: accounts, dashboard, register, settings, trade, wallet. Nav matches those exactly. So pages/nav actually match.

So the only real bug: missing `setTf` function. Let me add it. It should set `state.tf`, reseed history with the new timeframe, update active pill, and redraw.

Also, `drawCharts` uses `varCss('--accent')` — `varCss` is defined after `drawChartPrice` uses it? Function hoisting: `varCss` is a function declaration, hoisted. OK.

`ctx.setTransform(dpr,0,0,dpr,0,0)` then `ctx.fillText` — fine.

Let me add `setTf` function and re-check. Also add `window.setTf = setTf` so onclick in HTML can find it (onclick handlers resolve against window, and function declarations at top level of the IIFE? Wait — the whole script is wrapped in an IIFE: `<script>(function(){...})()`. My function declarations like `function setTf` — are they inside the IIFE? Looking at the written code: the script starts with `(function(){` at the end... wait no.

Looking at my written HTML: the script block begins with `/* ================= STATE ================= */ const DEMO=...` — NOT wrapped in IIFE! I removed the IIFE wrapper. So all functions are global. Good, onclick resolves them.

But wait, I have `let tickTimer` etc. at top level — fine.

